> > for {la. ... .} expressions or would that introduce a new confusion
> > where people, asked for their names, gave things that astarted with
> > {la} and ended witha pause?
>
> No, that would be most likely be incorrect. The x1 of cmene (also
> cmevla) *is* the text, it says so clearly in the definition.
>
> =E2=80=9Cla uuZIT cu cmene=E2=80=9D
> means that there is a name /which goes by the name =E2=80=9CuuZIT=E2=80=
=9D/.
> Yes, you say that the name has a name. xD
> This is almost certainly wrong unless this is what you actually wanted
> to say.
>
> =E2=80=9Czo uuZIT cu cmene=E2=80=9D
> in turn means that the word =E2=80=9CuuZIT=E2=80=9D is a name. This is co=
rrect. It is
> my name (in Lojban). :-)
>
> This is a known pitfall when using the word =E2=80=9Ccmene=E2=80=9D. See =
also:
> http://www.lojban.org/tiki/White+Knight%27s+Song+Gotcha
